{
  "_comment": [
    "The Tier 0 concept set. This is the SEED, not the output.",
    "",
    "The first harvester bulk-scanned every en-XX pair and filtered with keywords. It found",
    "declarative chat -- 'Dia lapar' (He is hungry), 'Air mengalir' (Water flows), 'The",
    "folder caught fire' -- because a keyword filter cannot tell a sentence a traveller",
    "UTTERS from a sentence that merely mentions a travel object.",
    "",
    "So the search is inverted. Instead of downloading everything and filtering, each",
    "concept is queried directly against the English side of the bitext, and only sentences",
    "that express THAT concept come back. Volume collapses; precision is total.",
    "",
    "`en_forms` are search strings sent to Tatoeba. They are English because the English",
    "side of the pair is where the concept is legible. `expect` is the shape a phrasebook",
    "line should take, used only to warn during selection -- never to reject silently."
  ],
